From: Henrique Carvalho <henrique.carvalho@suse.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 17:34:37 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] smb: client: fix change notify replay double-free
References: bsc#1258210
Patch-mainline: 6.18.39
Git-commit: 145f820dcbb2cced374f2532f8a61a44dce4a615

commit 145f820dcbb2cced374f2532f8a61a44dce4a615 upstream.

A response-bearing attempt can return a replayable error and free its
response buffer. If SMB2_notify_init() fails before the next send, cleanup
retains the previous buffer type and frees that response again.

Reset response bookkeeping before each attempt to prevent the stale free.

Fixes: 4f1fffa23769 ("cifs: commands that are retried should have replay flag set")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Henrique Carvalho <henrique.carvalho@suse.com>
Signed-off-by: Steve French <stfrench@microsoft.com>
Signed-off-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman <gregkh@linuxfoundation.org>
Signed-off-by: Robert Frohl <rfrohl@suse.com>
---
 fs/smb/client/smb2pdu.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/fs/smb/client/smb2pdu.c b/fs/smb/client/smb2pdu.c
index 486aa302ad0c..e6c4b5498f9e 100644
--- a/fs/smb/client/smb2pdu.c
+++ b/fs/smb/client/smb2pdu.c
@@ -4010,6 +4010,8 @@ SMB2_change_notify(const unsigned int xid, struct cifs_tcon *tcon,
 
 replay_again:
 	/* reinitialize for possible replay */
+	resp_buftype = CIFS_NO_BUFFER;
+	memset(&rsp_iov, 0, sizeof(rsp_iov));
 	flags = 0;
 	server = cifs_pick_channel(ses);
 
-- 
